\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nreasoning: The previous step listed services, but to identify faulty microservices, I need to check the actual pod statuses and deployments. Running `kubectl get pods` in the namespace will reveal if any pods are in error states (e.g., CrashLoopBackOff, Error), which directly indicates faults. This is critical for pinpointing failing components before deeper analysis.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=498, prompt_tokens=2682, total_tokens=3180, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cff23-caed-72c3-a259-1547417ebd06-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2682, 'output_tokens': 498, 'total_tokens': 3180}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='b3cede29-516d-4d2c-9078-04dc6d15d36c')]]
