s. They checked the logs for the geo pod, and the logs look normal—no errors, just informational messages. The pod started successfully, connected to the database, and registered with Consul.\n\nHmm, since the geo pod's logs don't show any issues, maybe the problem isn't with geo itself. The next step is to check the other pods that have restarts. Let's look at the next pod with restarts. The user mentioned pods like profile, rate, recommendation, reservation. Let's pick one of them, maybe the profile pod. Using kubectl logs on profile-69cb98cb67-47sxz to check its logs. If the logs for profile show errors, that could indicate a problem. If not, maybe check the deployment or replica set for that service to see if there are any configuration issues. Alternatively, check the dependencies of those pods, like the databases they're connecting to, or services like Consul and Jaeger. Maybe there's a network issue or a misconfiguration in the environment variables. Also, checking the metrics with get_metrics could help identify if there are any performance issues or resource constraints. But first, checking the logs of the next pod with restarts would be logical. If the logs are clean, then maybe look into the deployments or check for resource limits. Another possibility is that the pods are crashing due to a missing dependency, like a database not being available. So, checking the logs of the profile pod next makes sense.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nreasoning: The geo pod logs show no errors, so I need to investigate other pods with restarts (profile, rate, recommendation, reservation). Checking the logs for the **profile** pod next will help identify if it's experiencing similar issues. If its logs are clean, I'll proceed to check deployments or resource constraints. If errors are present, they may indicate misconfigurations, dependency failures, or application crashes.", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 462, 'prompt_tokens': 5211, 'total_tokens': 5673, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cff24-1a6d-7c40-99c9-e9c879ecb396-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5211, 'output_tokens': 462, 'total_tokens': 5673}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='dccc2ebc-91c9-4a3b-aa8b-1b1b98e4b8bc'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagnose issues in the hotel reservation application, which consists of many microservices. So far, they\'ve checked the services and pods, and found that some pods like geo, profile, rate, recommendation, and reservation have non-zero restarts. They checked the geo pod\'s logs and didn\'t find any errors. Now they need to check the next pod with restarts, which is the profile pod.\n\nThe next logical step is to look into the profile pod\'s logs to see if there are any error messages or issues causing it to restart. If the profile pod\'s logs are also clean, then maybe the problem is elsewhere, like in the deployments or resource constraints. But if there are errors in the logs, that could point to specific issues such as misconfigurations, failed dependencies, or application crashes.\n\nSo, the tool to use here is exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd with the command to get the logs of the profile pod. The command would be "kubectl logs profile-69cb98cb67-47sxz -n hotel-reservation". This will retrieve the logs for the profile pod, allowing the user to check for any errors or exceptions that might be causing the restarts. If the logs are free of errors, then the next step might involve checking the deployments, replica sets, or resource limits. But for now, checking the logs is the immediate next action.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs profile-69cb98cb67-47sxz -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a2a7868ee88e14f2', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 341, 'prompt_tokens': 6211, 'total_tokens': 6552, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cff24-309a-7e81-90e2-53edb1fbae8e-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs profile-69cb98cb67-47sxz -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a2a7868ee88e14f2', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6211, 'output_tokens': 341, 'total_tokens': 6552}), ToolMessage(content='{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-18T04:08:59Z","message":"TLS disabled."}\n{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-18T04:08:59Z","message":"Set global log level: info"}\n{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-18T04:08:59Z","message":"Tune: setGCPercent to 100"}\n\x1b[90m2026-03-18T04:08:59Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/profile/main.go:24\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mReading config...\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-18T04:08:59Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/profile/main.go:37\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mRead database URL: mongodb-profile:27017\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-18T04:08:59Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/profile/main.go:38\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mInitializing DB connection...\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-18T04:08:59Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/profile/db.go:36\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mNew session successfull...\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-18T04:08:59Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/profile/db.go:38\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mGen