tarts. Let\'s pick one of them, maybe the geo pod, and check its logs. If there are errors in the logs, that could indicate the root cause. Alternatively, maybe the issue is with the deployments or replicasets. But since the pods are running, maybe the problem is with the application code or external dependencies.\n\nAnother approach could be to check the metrics using get_metrics to see if there are any anomalies, like high error rates or latency. But first, checking the logs would give direct insight into what\'s going wrong. So, the next step is to get the logs for the pods with restarts.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nreasoning: Several pods (geo, profile, rate, recommendation, reservation) have non-zero restarts. To identify the root cause, I need to inspect their logs for errors or exceptions. Using `kubectl logs` on these pods will reveal application-level issues, such as crashes, failed dependencies, or misconfigurations. This is critical for diagnosing why pods are restarting despite being in "Running" state.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 406, 'prompt_tokens': 3567, 'total_tokens': 3973, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cff23-eff4-7ab0-abdb-7776e1c8c560-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3567, 'output_tokens': 406, 'total_tokens': 3973}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='ed408fb4-bd3e-4c6f-b03e-4917fcf9312c'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagnose faults in the hotel reservation application. They\'ve already checked the services and pods, and noticed some pods have restarts. The next step is to look into the logs of those pods to find out why they\'re restarting.\n\nThe pods with restarts are geo, profile, rate, recommendation, reservation. The user needs to check their logs. The tool available is exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd, which can run kubectl logs. But since there are multiple pods, maybe they should start with one. However, the user might want to check all of them. Wait, but the tool call can only handle one command at a time. So maybe the assistant should pick one pod first, like the geo pod, to check its logs. Alternatively, maybe the user should check all pods with restarts. But the tool requires specifying a command. The command for logs is "kubectl logs [pod-name] -n [namespace]". So the assistant needs to choose a specific pod. Let me check the previous output again. The pods with restarts are geo-57c7bd6d5c-fcxlc (2 restarts), profile-69cb98cb67-47sxz (2), rate-6fff88f6f5-jlqgj (2), recommendation-64754c9c4f-9kgzp (2), reservation-7bb77b596b-hmwnb (2). Maybe start with the geo pod. So the command would be "kubectl logs geo-57c7bd6d5c-fcxlc -n hotel-reservation". That\'s the next step. The reasoning is to check the logs for errors causing restarts.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs geo-57c7bd6d5c-fcxlc -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b8b1098f2c0d15bb', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 416, 'prompt_tokens': 4565, 'total_tokens': 4981, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cff24-0393-7c11-bafb-37e3b3ec04d7-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs geo-57c7bd6d5c-fcxlc -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'ch